WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.387
Normalization helps reduce repeated facts and the
anomalies they can create An

00:00:06.413 --> 00:00:09.874
update anomaly occurs when the same fact appears in
many rows and

00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:15.650
the copies become inconsistent An insertion anomaly
occurs when you cannot

00:00:15.677 --> 00:00:21.325
store one fact without inventing another unrelated
fact A deletion

00:00:21.351 --> 00:00:25.759
anomaly occurs when removing one record accidentally
removes the only copy of

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:31.244
some other important information The general goal is
to store each fact

00:00:31.257 --> 00:00:36.800
in a place that matches what determines that fact
Normalization is not

00:00:36.813 --> 00:00:41.513
about splitting tables into as many pieces as
possible It is about

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.579
making dependencies clearer so updates inserts and
deletes do not accidentally damage

00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:47.961
unrelated information
